 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "RingBuffer(capacity) owns capacity cells, a write pointer and a read pointer (both start at 0) and an unread counter. Each character is one byte. write(data) stores each character at the write pointer and advances it modulo capacity; the unread counter grows by one per character up to capacity, and the read pointer does not move even when unread data is overwritten. read(n) returns min(n, unread) characters starting at the read pointer (wrapping), advances the read pointer by that many and decreases the unread counter. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
